WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.900
This slide summarizes the normalization progression
First Normal Form

00:00:05.914 --> 00:00:10.348
removes repeating groups and list-like values so
each field represents one value

00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:16.652
Second Normal Form handles partial dependencies when
a composite key is involved

00:00:17.576 --> 00:00:22.753
Facts that depend on only part of that key move
elsewhere Third

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:26.950
Normal Form removes transitive dependencies so
non-key facts are stored with the

00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:32.478
entity that actually determines them A fast
diagnostic is to ask how

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:37.951
many rows must change when one fact changes If
changing a patient's

00:00:37.965 --> 00:00:43.083
name requires updating many appointment-service rows
patient information is probably stored in

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:48.798
the wrong place In a well-designed operational
schema one patient fact

00:00:48.812 --> 00:00:51.325
should usually be updated in one patient row
